Z||000000||NorthernFiero||10-21-2001||10:20 PM||||Do they make a T-Top for a Fiero where the T bar can be removed? I saw it on my Ex girlfriends ricer thought it would be cool on my Fiero. If they do where can I get one.<P>thanks,<BR>Mike||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-22-2001||07:19 PM||||There have been a few Fiero owners who have done a Targa top (which is what you're talking about).  It takes a lot of work, though.  You have to add bracing to the frame (either C channels or an X brace) as well as manufacturing all of the parts and pieces on your own as there isn't a commercially available kit as far as I know.  This would include the top itself as well as a fastening system and all of the new trim.  You might want to do a search for Cozmo.  I think he did a Targa on his Fiero.||||reg||1
